{
"opening": "The following changes enhance the robustness and consistency of the iterutils module, specifically addressing recursion safety in remap and research, and correcting edge-case behavior in split. These updates ensure that circular data structures are handled gracefully and that utility functions behave predictably across all input parameters.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m01",
"text": "The `remap` function must accept a `cache` argument to track visited objects, thereby preventing infinite recursion on circular structures and ensuring repeated references are mapped only once."
},
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "The `research` function must accept a `cache` argument and forward it to internal calls to `remap`, allowing users to handle circular structures consistently during path traversal."
},
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "The `split` function must return the values from the source iterable when `maxsplit` is zero, rather than wrapping or returning the original source object itself."
}
]
}
